{"assets":["/statement-assets/b5c5540605e412deedb3eddfa771a202c410ff53d13500489880fe108290bb1e.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1170","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Graph Decomposition"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"6 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an undirected graph consisting of $$$n$$$ vertices and $$$m$$$ edges."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall that a cycle is a path that starts and ends in the same vertex. A cycle in a graph is called simple if it contains each vertex (except the starting and ending one) no more than once (the starting and the ending one is contained always "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"twice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Note that loops are considered to be simple cycles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one move you can choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" simple cycle in this graph and erase the edges corresponding to this cycle (corresponding vertices remain in the graph). It is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"allowed"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to erase the loop or two copies of the same edge (take a look at examples)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your problem is to apply some sequence of moves to obtain the graph without edges. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is not necessary to minimize the number of cycles"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". If it is impossible, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of vertices and the number of edges in the graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next $$$m$$$ lines contain edges of the graph. The $$$i$$$-th line contains the $$$i$$$-th edge $$$x_i, y_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le x_i, y_i \\le n$$$), where $$$x_i$$$ and $$$y_i$$$ are vertices connected by the $$$i$$$-th edge. The graph "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"can contain loops or multiple edges"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is impossible to decompose the given graph into simple cycles, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in the first line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in the first line. In the second line print $$$k$$$ — the number of simple cycles in the graph decomposition."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the next $$$k$$$ lines print cycles themselves. The $$$j$$$-th line should contain the $$$j$$$-th cycle. First, print $$$c_j$$$ — the number of vertices in the $$$j$$$-th cycle. Then print the cycle as a sequence of vertices. All neighbouring (adjacent) vertices in the printed path should be connected by an edge that isn't contained in other cycles."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 9\n1 2\n2 3\n1 3\n2 4\n2 5\n4 5\n3 5\n3 6\n5 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\n3\n4 2 5 4 2 \n4 3 6 5 3 \n4 1 3 2 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 7\n1 1\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 1\n1 3\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\n3\n2 1 1 \n5 1 4 3 2 1 \n3 1 3 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 8\n1 1\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 1\n2 4\n1 3\n1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The picture corresponding to the first example: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b5c5540605e412deedb3eddfa771a202c410ff53d13500489880fe108290bb1e.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"1170G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1170/problem/G"}